east   The immunoperoxidase studies would be consistent with a poorly  differentiated breast carcinoma  although the results do not exclude other  primary sites   Clinical and radiologic correlation is suggested   CLINICAL DATA   History  67 year old post menopausal woman  not on HRT with positive mammogram  right at outside hospital REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy showed DCIS  also had enlarged  lymph nodes  right axilla  breast excision REMOVED_DATE showed DCIS  possible  invasion  REMOVED_DATE axillary nodes positive for mets  since mammographic lesion very  small and path showed only DCIS  but multiple nodes involved question possible  secondary primary metastatic to lymph nodes   Operation  Right breast wire localized lumpectomy  axillary biopsy  Clinical Diagnosis  Right breast cancer  metastatic right axillary lymph nodes  TISSUE SUBMITTED  Consult slides  GROSS DESCRIPTION  by PREISINGER ELIZABETH ANN M D   Received from Hallmark Health Lawrence Memorial Hospital  Department of  Pathology  170 Governors Avenue  Medford  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  are forty five  45  slides   Four  4  slides are labeled   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    sublabeled  A  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     B  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     C  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    and   D  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    corresponding to right stereotactic breast biopsy obtained on REMOVED_DATE   according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient s name   Forty one  41  slides are labeled   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    sublabeled  1A  trhough  1F    1H   through  1V    2A  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   through  2F    2D ER   control    2D PR   control    2  Her2 neu    2D CEA   control    2D  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    control    2D  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    control    2D   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    control    2D CA 125   control    2D WT   control    2D  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    control     2D Vim   control    2D HMFG 2   control    2D TTF 1   control s  and  2D  negative   corresponding to 1  right breast biopsy  needle localization  for 