Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel  617  REMOVED_DATE    Molecular Pathology Report  PDGFRA FISH Analysis      Accession     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  J   DOB  REMOVED_DATE  Age  69   Sex  F  MRN   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Institution  MGH  Location   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   BRAIN TUMOR CTR  Date of Collection  REMOVED_DATE  Date of Accession  REMOVED_DATE  Reported  REMOVED_DATE 22 45  Results To   Andrew S  Chi MD  PhD      CLINICAL HISTORY   Brain Astrocytoma    SPECIMENS RECEIVED   A  Molecular test for PDGFRA    SLIDE BLOCK DESCRIPTION    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID               TEST PERFORMED   PDGFRA FISH ANALYSIS    INDICATION FOR TEST Brain Astrocytoma    RESULTS    Platelet Derived Growth Factor Receptor Alpha  PDGFRA  gene amplification   PDGFRA  Reference Probe Copy Number Ratio  REMOVED_DATE    INTERPRETATION   The FISH data are consistent with NO amplification of the PDGFRA gene  block   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID       TEST INFORMATION   Platelet derived growth factor receptor alpha  PDGFRA  is a receptor tyrosine  kinase implicated in the tumorigenesis of human cancers  Amplification of the  PDGFRA gene has been identified in various human neoplasms including lung  squamous cell carcinoma and glioblastoma multiforme and is a characteristic of  the  proneural  subtype of glioblastoma   1 2     The assay performed on this patient uses fluorescence in situ hybridization   FISH  on formalin fixed paraffin embedded tumor specimens to analyze PDGFRA  gene amplification status  Briefly  5 micron sections of formalin fixed  paraffin embedded tumor material were prepared and an H E section reviewed to  select regions for hybridization that contain a majority of tumor cells  A  dual color FISH assay was performed using Bacterial Artificial Chromosome probe   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   chromosome 4q12  PDGFRA locus  and a copy number control  centromere  4  Cep4  Abbott Vysis 06 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      Signal quantitation was used to generate a PDGFRA centromere 4 ratio  PDGFRA to  Centromere 4 ratios are interpreted as follows  REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE is considered  borderline for amplification  REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE is considered low level amplification   and greater than REMOVED_DATE or clustered signals that are too numerous to count would  be considered highly amplified  CPT codes for this assay are  REMOVED_CASE_ID  x 2     References  1  Ramos AH  et al  Amplification of chromosomal segment 4q12 in  non small cell lung cancer  Cancer Biol Ther   REMOVED_CASE_ID  Nov 8 21   REMOVED_CASE_ID  50   2  Verhaak RG  et al  Integrated genomic analysis identifies clinically  relevant subtypes of glioblastoma characterized by abnormalities in PDGFRA    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   EGFR  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cancer Cell   REMOVED_CASE_ID  17 1  98 110     This test was developed  and its performance characteristics were determined by  the MGH Diagnostic Molecular Pathology Laboratory  It has not been cleared or  approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  The FDA has determined that  such clearance or approval is not necessary  This test is used for clinical  purposes  Pursuant to the requirements of CLIA  88  this laboratory has  established and verified the test s accuracy and precision     Questions concerning these values should be addressed to Dr  A  John Iafrate at   617  REMOVED_DATE MGH internal address  Diagnostic Molecular Pathology Laboratory   Massachusetts General Hospital  55 Fruit St   Warren 508  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID             Electronically Signed Out By  Anthony John Iafrate MD         PART   Molecular test for PDGFRA       report_end  , Negative.
