Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  19 MAY 94 ACCESSIONED ON  19 MAY 94 at 17 10 CLINICAL DATA  Clinical picture consistent with inflammatory breast ca  status post left lumpectomy and radiation therapy in  REMOVED_CASE_ID   Unable to diagnose malignancy on prior FNA or open biopsy in REMOVED_DATE                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY    INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  85    AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  15     SEE NOTE    INTERSTITIAL AND INTIMAL FIBROSIS AND CYTOLOGICAL ATYPIA  CONSISTENT WITH RADIATION EFFECT  NOTE  No definite vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  Marked radiation atypia excludes cytologic grading of the tumor  Resection margins and the size of the tumor cannot be evaluated due to fragmentation of the specimen  Diagnosis by  Volker Nickeleit  M D  Signed On  23 MAY 94 at 17 21                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 MAY 94 at 07 33 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  are three fragments of yellow tan firm tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x 3 x 2 8cm in aggregate  A portion of one is frozen as frozen section  1  and kept frozen  Remainder of tissue submitted in A through E  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Thomas J Lynch  M D  John Ellery Munzenrider  M D  PART   BREAST  BIOPSY  LEFT    report_end  , Negative.
