Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  WCP Breast Onc  YAW 9 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  IRENE KUTER  M D  PHOEBE E FREER  M D  Resident  Jill Ono  M D  Signed Out by  Melinda J Lerwill  M D  CLINICAL DATA  32 year old female with history of right breast locally advanced cancer in  REMOVED_CASE_ID   now with tiny 7mm enhancing bilobed nodule on MRI  no mammographic or sonographic correlate    FBA versus lymph node versus CA   FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY  PROLIFERATIVE SCLEROSING LESION  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The lesion may represent either a sclerosing papilloma or adenomyoepithelioma  Cytokeratin REMOVED_DATE immunostains are positive in the superimposed epithelial proliferation  most consistent with florid usual ductal hyperplasia  There is some mild cellular enlargement that is favored to represent a reactive alteration  Based on the pattern of staining for cytokeratin REMOVED_DATE and smooth muscle myosin heavy chain  there is a possibility of a proliferative myoepithelial component in the lesion  raising consideration of an adenomyoepithelioma  p63 is not co immunoreactive in the areas of myosin positivity  however  and the histologic findings are not definitive for the presence of a second cell type  Peripheral myoepithelial cells are identified around the lesion on p63 and smooth muscle myosin heavy chain immunostains  although they are diminished in number around the most proliferative area  Multiple levels examined  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN only  are 8 cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE