ur archives of that case is  compared to the current breast lesion and the morphology is similar  although  only the immunoperoxidase studies are available for review   This current  breast lesion shows neuroendocrine differentiation  NSE  synaptophysin and  chromogranin positivity   and thus likely represents metastatic neuroendocrine  tumor similar to that in the patient s mandible in  REMOVED_CASE_ID    CLINICAL DATA   HISTORY  47 year old female with history of carcinoid metastatic to liver and  bone with carcinoid syndrome  New right breast 10 00 mass   cancer  Right  lower outer quadrant calcifications   BREAST IMAGING FINDING   1  Right  6mm  Nonpalpable and irregular mass   2  Right  1cm  Nonpalpable calcifications   LOCATION   1  Right   2  Right  Lower outer   TYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY   1  14 G Ultrasound  2  8 G Stereotactic  TISSUE SUBMITTED   1  14G Ultrasound 5   Pink cassette   2  8 G Ultrasound 4   Green cassettes  A   Calcs  B   No calcs   GROSS DESCRIPTION   The specimen is received in formalin  in two parts  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   patient s name  unit number   Part A   right breast  10 o clock mass   and consists of one pink cassette   right  containing mostly pink tan tissues  1 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm in aggregate    Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Pink cassette contents  multi frags  ESS   Part B   right breast lower outer calc   and consists of two fresh green  cassettes  A CA    contains mostly yellow tan to pink tan soft tissues  2 2 x  0 9 x 0 4cm in aggregate   Second green cassette  B   and contains mostly  yellow tan to pink red soft tissues  1 9 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm in aggregate    Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Green cassette A contents  CA     multi frags  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Green cassette B contents  multi frags  ESS   CASE NUMBER  BS 07  REMOVED_CASE_ID    lm ag  By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she  personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if