uscle  and a 3 8cm in diameter defect which extends to the subjacent biopsy cavity which measures 3 2cm in diameter  The cavity is located 1 9cm to the superior margin  6 5cm to the inferior margin  10 5cm to the medial margin  and extends to the deep margin  The cavity is surrounded by firm  tan tissue  No masses or nodules are grossly identified  The remainder of the tissue consists predominantly  70   of soft  lobulated yellow tan adipose tissue with soft  intervening  white fibrous tissue  On sectioning through the attached axillary adipose tissue  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm firm region which is focally cystic and hemorrhagic  This area is located beneath the smaller incision site at one end of the skin ellipse  Several lymph node candidates are identified in the attached axillary adipose tissue which measure up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The lymph nodes have soft  yellow cut surfaces  Representative sections are submitted as   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity with overlying skin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity with deep margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nipple bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   En face section at base of nipple   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lesions in axillary fat   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two intact lymph node candidates   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected lymph node in two cassettes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One trisected lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two sections away from biopsy cavity  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm unoriented irregular portion of adipose tissue  Several lymph nodes are located in the adipose tissue which measure up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm  The smaller nodes have soft  tan brown cut surfaces  The largest node has firm  tan white cut surfaces  The lymph nodes