ies the specimen showing a needle with a possible microcalcifications   Because the specimen is unoriented  it is inked all in one color  The needle  tip went through one piece of the tissue which fell off the specimen prior to  inking  This portion of tissue is submitted separately but is not inked  On  sectioning the specimen is 75  adipose  There is a white fibrous area  measuring 3cm x 3 x 1 5cm which contains areas of hemorrhage  This could  represent the prior biopsy site  Note that the white fibrous area borders the  blue inked margin   Micro 1  tissue at needle tip  1 frag  ESS   Micro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue submitted from area far from potential biopsy cavity  to fibrous area with potential biopsy cavity  multi frags  ESS   Part two   extra left breast tissue   consisting of four unoriented fragments  of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1cm REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 1 2cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x  0 5cm  and REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 5cm  Each of the fragments was inked blue  On  sectioning some of the fragments are primarily fibrous with hemorrhagic areas   Micro 18  1 fragment  bisected  2 frags  ESS   Micro 19  1 fragment with fibrous hemorrhagic area  3 frags  ESS   Micro 20  1 fragment  bisected  2 frags  ESS   Micro 21 22  4 fragments fibrous areas  5 frags  ESS   ref  Reports to  RHEI  ESTHER M D   SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST   EXCISIONAL TISSUE W MARGINS  ADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE  SURGICAL MARGIN   report_end  , Unknown.
