Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  28 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  28 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 59 CLINICAL DATA  Excision  right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM   90   MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 2 3   PRESENT WITHIN 1MM OF AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  NO VASCULAR IS IDENTIFIED  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  10   WITH CANCERIZATION OF LOBULES  SEE NOTE  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FOCAL ATYPICAL HYPERPLASIA AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA  NOTE  The majority of the in situ component is located within or adjacent to the main mass  however small foci are at a distance from it    Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D  Signed On  02 MAY 95 at 14 50                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  