ections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 06 50 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two pieces of breast tissue  The first specimen is designated  Superior specimen left breast  and is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm breast tissue fragment  It is inked and sectioned to reveal numerous small cysts up to 0 3cm in greatest dimension  Fully submitted in formalin in A F  Labeled  Inferior specimen left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm breast tissue fragment  which is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 9cm white firm area with irregular borders suspicious for carcinoma  Sections for formalin are submitted in G through N  Cassettes H  I  and J include the suspicious sections  Fully submitted  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DX  BREAST  INFERIOR LEFT   REMOVED_DATE CM NODULE SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LEFT BREAST  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Negative.
