aspiration clinic by Connie Roche NP for consultation and diagnosis of right  axillary nodules     Clinical History  History of invasive ductal carcinoma of the left breast   excised in  REMOVED_CASE_ID   now with axillary nodules in area of surgical site  Prior  biopsy  FNA  of this area was non diagnostic  1 24 13      Review of Symptoms   Constitutional  Well appearing adult female     Review of Patient Data   Radiology  REMOVED_DATE mammogram and ultrasound   Past histology  REMOVED_DATE right axilla FNA   Office Notes  REMOVED_DATE reviewed    Physical Examination  Laterality was established according to departmental  universal protocol  Examination of the right axilla reveals 3 nodules   Anterior nodule  0 5cm well defined  soft  mobile   Lateral nodule  0 5cm  poorly defined  soft   Posterior nodule    0 5cm  soft  poorly defined   All nodules were mobile and in the surgical site in the patient s axilla  All  3 nodules biopsied but posterior nodule biopsy aborted due to patient  discomfort     Assessment  Based on the clinical history and physical examination  FNAB is  warranted     Procedure  The procedure and complications were explained to the patient and  verbal consent was obtained     Site 1  2 aspirates were performed of the anterior nodule using 25 gauge needles  without anesthesia and without complications  3 slides were stained for  immediate evaluation  additional tissue was submitted for further evaluation     Site 2  2 aspirates were performed of the lateral nodule using 25 gauge needles  without anesthesia and without complications  3 slides were stained for  immediate evaluation  additional tissue was submitted for further evaluation     Disposition  The immediate interpretation findings were discussed with the  patient  The preliminary results were communicated to Connie Roche at 4o clock  P M         The signing pathologist attests that he she performed the procedure or  if  performed by a resident or fellow  directed and supervised the FNA procedure and  was immediately available to further assist the resident fellow before  during  and after the procedure  and has reviewed and confirmed the interpretation of  slides stained for immediate evaluation            Electronically Signed Out By  Rosemary H Tambouret MD on REMOVED_DATE 12 36       CLINICAL HISTORY  54 year old female with a history of IDC status post lumpectomy on right side   Now with nodules in prior surgical site         SPECIMEN SOURCE  A  AXILLA FNA BIOPSY  RIGHT  1  B  AXILLA FNA BIOPSY  RIGHT  2    GROSS DESCRIPTION  A  AXILLA FNA BIOPSY  RIGHT  1  Received 1 slides in ETOH  3 air dried smears  and 4ml clear  colorless fluid for 1 surepath slide     B  AXILLA FNA BIOPSY  RIGHT  2  Received 1 slides in ETOH  3 air dried smears  and 4ml pink fluid for 1 surepath slide           Specimen  AXILLA FNA BIOPSY  RIGHT  1  Specimen  AXILLA FNA BIOPSY  RIGHT  2       report_end  , Negative.
