Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  23 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 01 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY 1  INVASIVE MAMMARY CARCINOMA  LESS THAN 0 2CM   SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE WITH CANCERIZATION OF LOBULES  COMEDO TYPE NECROSIS AND MICROCALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  The invasive carcinoma consists of malignant cells permeating stroma in a single cell fashion  The small size of the invasive mammary carcinoma precludes accurate classification into ductal or lobular type  If one were to grade this as a ductal type  it would be low grade  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 58                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number are nine cores of soft  tan tissue  ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm which are submitted in toto in cassette A  Gross Description by  Jason Corbin Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Ashby Carter Moncure  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSIES   report_end  , Unknown.
