Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 32 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast biopsy 10 years ago  now 2 abnormal areas on mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT UPPER OVER QUADRANT LESION   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENITATED   0 9 CM   EXTENDING TO INKED MARGIN WITH PERINEURAL INVASION  80    WITH INTRADUCTAL COMPONENT  20    MICROCALCIFICATIONS  BREAST  LEFT  2   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED   LESS THAN 1 CM   EXTENDING TO WITHIN 1MM OF INKED MARGIN  2  MULTICENTRIC INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA WITH FOCAL CANCERIZATION OF LOBULES  EXTENDING TO LESS THAN 1MM OF INKED MARGIN  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 24                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 51 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  1  upper outer quadrant lesion  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm piece of breast tissue with localizing wire in place  The mammogram accompanies the specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal two firm foci each less than 1cm in size  One focus is submitted in A and B  the other in C through E  and the remainder of this specimen in F through J  No frozen section performed  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  2  are a 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm piece of breast with localizing wire and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm piece of breast  The larger specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal several irregular firm foci each less than 1cm in diameter  submitted in K through L  and the remainder submitted in M through S  The smaller fragment is inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast tissue  all submitted in T through U  No frozen section done  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS   1 LEFT BREAST   NO LESION LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE  GROSS DIAGNOSIS   2 LEFT BREAST   NO LESION LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Lisa H  Lerner  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                            