CRIPTION  Received fresh and  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast biopsy with needle localization  long stitch lateral  short stitch superior   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm fragment of breast tissue with a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral  The needle localization wire is in place  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior blue  posterior black  superior green and inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral resection margin  The breast parenchyma consists of admixed fatty tissue and dense pink white fibrous stroma  An obvious tumor is not identified  Submitted entirely from medial to lateral resection margins in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  representing the medial end margin and cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  representing the lateral end margin  and cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  representing the area designated by needle localization wire  Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday May 27   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01 57 12PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows    The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained    Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained    Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained    The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  These tests were develo