ce     TEST INFORMATION   In recent years  major efforts to define the molecular causes of cancer have  revealed a wide number of genetic aberrations  A small subset of these defects   usually referred to as  drivers   is frequently present across cancer types and  appears to be essential for oncogenesis and tumor progression  New drugs  developed to selectively target such cancer promoting pathways  are starting to  complement the more conventional therapeutic approaches  While the clinical  benefit observed with some targeted agents is encouraging  it has become clear  that for such strategies to be successful  it will be necessary to identify the  patient population carrying the genetic abnormalities targeted by each drug     We have developed a multiplexed allele specific assay to detect somatic  mutations in tumor DNA extracted from formalin fixed paraffin embedded samples   Dias Santagata  REMOVED_CASE_ID    The assay SNaPshot Version 3 detects mutations in 68  different loci from 14 cancer genes  Briefly  multiplex PCR using tumor DNA is  followed by mutation detection using single base extension sequencing technology   SNaPshot  Applied Biosystems   In addition  a separate PCR reaction using  primers flanking EGFR exon 19  EGFR exon 20 and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  exon 20 are used to detect  in frame activating insertions or deletions in EGFR and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  that may not be  detected using SNaPshot  The mutations are visualized using an ABI  REMOVED_CASE_ID  DNA  analyzer  The average analytic sensitivity of detecting mutations in this assay  has been established in our laboratory at approximately 5  mutant allele     REFERENCES   Dias Santagata D  Akhavanfard S  David SS  Vernovsky K  Kuhlmann G  Boisvert SL   Stubbs H  McDermott U  Settleman J  Kwak EL  Clark JW  Isakoff SJ  Sequist LV   Engelman JA  Lynch TJ  Haber DA  Louis DN  Ellisen LW  Borger DR  Iafrate AJ    REMOVED_CASE_ID   Rapid targeted mutational analysis of human tumours  a clinical platform  to guide personalized cancer medicine  EMBO Mol Med  2 5  146 58   Ladanyi M  Pao W   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Lung adenocarcinoma  guiding EGFR targeted therapy and  beyond  Mod  Pathol  21 Suppl 2  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      This test was developed  and its performance characteristics were determined by  the MGH Diagnostic Molecular Pathology Laboratory  It has not been approved by  the U S  Food and Drug Administration  The FDA has determined that such  clearance is not necessary  This test is used for clinical purposes  Pursuant to  the requirements of CLIA 88  this laboratory has established and verified the  test accuracy and precision     Question concerning these values should be addressed to Dr  A  John Iafrate at   617 726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   MGH internal address  MGH Diagnostic Molecular Pathology  Laboratory  Massachusetts General Hospital  70 Blossom Street  GRJ  REMOVED_CASE_ID   Boston   MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID             Electronically Signed Out By  Anthony John Iafrate MD         PART   Molecular test for SNAPSHOT       report_end  , Negative.
