nodule  anxious    Physical Exam  The right chest wall showed a 2cm  non tender  ill defined   ovoid  firm  and fixed mass     Ultrasound was used to evaluate the lesion and showed a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm  lesion that was ill defined  irregular  solid and cystic  wider than tall   heterogeneously hypoechoic  without significant internal vascularity  and  without notable peripheral vascularity     Assessment  Based on the clinical history and physical examination  an FNAB is  warranted     Procedure  The procedure and potential complications were explained to the  patient  who understood the purpose  risks  and benefits of the procedure  The  patient confirmed name  date of birth  laterality  and lesion to be aspirated   Written consent was obtained     The biopsy procedure was performed by palpation and under ultrasound guidance  due to insufficient cellularity with palpation biopsy  Both parallel and  perpendicular approaches to the nodule were performed with clear vision of the  needle in the lesion     6 aspirates were performed using 25 gauge needles without local anesthesia and  without complications   7 slides were stained for immediate evaluation  Additional tissue was submitted  for further evaluation     The procedure was performed by Roseann Wu  M D  and Martha Pitman  M D     Disposition  The immediate interpretation findings were discussed with the  patient  Connie Roche  NP was notified of the preliminary results by personal  communication at 2 50 p m         The signing pathologist attests that he she performed the procedure or  if  performed by a resident or fellow  directed and supervised the FNA procedure and  was immediately available to further assist the resident fellow before  during  and after the procedure  and has reviewed and confirmed the interpretation of  slides stained for immediate evaluation            Electronically Signed Out By  Martha Bishop Pitman MD on REMOVED_DATE 13 27       CLINICAL HISTORY  52 year old female with history of right breast IDC  Status post chemo  surgery   XRT         SPECIMEN SOURCE  A  FNA BIOPSY  CHEST WALL SOFT TISSUE    GROSS DESCRIPTION  A  FNA BIOPSY  CHEST WALL SOFT TISSUE  Received 2 slides in ETOH  Received 7  air dried slides           Specimen  FNA BIOPSY  CHEST WALL SOFT TISSUE       report_end  , Positive.
