V     Physical Examination  Laterality was established according to departmental  universal protocol  Examination of the right hip reveals a 3cm rounded  firm   subcutaneous nodule     Assessment  Based on the clinical history and physical examination  an FNAB is  warranted     Procedure  The procedure and complications were explained to the patient  the  patient confirmed name  date of birth and lesion to be aspirated  Written  consent was obtained  2 aspirates were performed using 23 and 25 gauge needles  with anesthesia and without complications  3 slides were stained for immediate  evaluation  additional tissue was submitted for further evaluation     Disposition  The preliminary results were communicated to Dr  Hughes in person  at 3 50 p m       The signing pathologist attests that he she performed the procedure or  if  performed by a resident or fellow  directed and supervised the FNA procedure and  was immediately available to further assist the resident fellow before  during  and after the procedure  and has reviewed and confirmed the interpretation of  slides stained for immediate evaluation            Electronically Signed Out By  Ivan A Chebib MD on REMOVED_DATE 11 58       CLINICAL HISTORY    42 year old female with right hip nodularity  history of free silicone  injection         SPECIMEN SOURCE  A  SUBCUTANEOUS MASS FNA BIOPSY  RIGHT HIP    GROSS DESCRIPTION  A  SUBCUTANEOUS MASS FNA BIOPSY  RIGHT HIP  Received 1 slide in ETOH  Received  2 air dried slides           Specimen  SUBCUTANEOUS MASS FNA BIOPSY  RIGHT HIP       report_end  , Positive.
