Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 REMOVED_MONTH 92 ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 92 at 11 50 CLINICAL DATA  Postmenopausal female with a 1 to 2cm round mobile mass in the medial portion of the right breast  No clinical axillary or supraclavicular adenopathy  A recent needle aspiration in office was interpreted as suspicious for carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1 OF 3  AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  WITH FEATURES OF NEUROENDOCRINE DIFFERENTIATION  SEE NOTE  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES INCLUDING FIBROSIS  CYSTS  APOCRINE METAPLASIA  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  AND MODERATE DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA WITH FOCAL ATYPICALITY  3  MICROCALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  No definite lymphatic and vascular invasion is identified  The tumor measures 1 5cm in greatest dimension and is less than 0 1cm from several inked margins  but because of its unusual architectural features  the relative quantities of the invasive and in situ components cannot be adequately assessed  Ductal carcinoma in situ is present at a distance of at least one low power microscopic field from the main tumor mass  Using immunoperoxidase methods on paraffin embedded  formalin fixed tissue  many tumor cells are positive for carcinoembryonic antigen  rare tumor cells are positive for synaptophysin  suggesting neuroendocrine differentiation  and tumor cells are negative for chromogranin  Tumor cells do not show argyrophil granules by the Grimelius method  Dr  Koerner has reviewed this case and agrees with the diagnosis  Unequivocal invasive carcinoma is not identified on the frozen section slide  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 28                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN   SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the corresponding values were 97  and 95   respectively  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 breast carcinomas with determination of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy nine percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 97  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 08     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 14 44 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is an excisional biopsy of fibrofatty breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a dark purple  nodular area surrounded by a firm white tissue  The nodule abuts the margin and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm  At the periphery is soft  white adipose tissue  A representative section is frozen as Frozen Section  1 and saved frozen for ancillary studies  Section Code  A J  nodule and breast biopsy K N  remainder of tissue  Resident  Rex Neal Smith  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  NO INVASION DEMONSTRATED  O R  Resident  Jo Ann E  Haney  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  David William Rattner  M D  Rex Neal Smith  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST TISSUE   report_end  , Negative.
