Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  WCP Breast Onc  YAW 9 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D  ELIZABETH A RAFFERTY  M D  Resident  Maylee Hsu  M D  Signed Out by  Robert Hasserjian  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Diagnostic Information CLINICAL DATA  Patient with known  L  breast cancer  Second lesion seen on MRI  Rule out malignancy  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY  BENIGN INTRAPARENCHYMAL LYMPH NODE  CLUSTER OF ATYPICAL KERATIN POSITIVE EPITHELIAL CELLS IN ADJACENT BLOOD CLOT  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The biopsy consists of lymphoid tissue  fibroadipose tissue  and blood clot  The lymphoid tissue appears to be a portion of lymph node with sinuses  venules  and a population of morphologically normal lymphocytes and histiocytes  Immunohistochemical stains show that the lymph node is composed of a few follicles of  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   B cells in a predominant background of  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   T cells   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  stains dendritic cells in the follicles and BCL 6 also stains a few cells in these regions   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  stains only rare cells  BCL 2 stains many cells  including both the follicles and the interfollicular areas  consistent with primary follicles  A Ki 67 stain is positive in approximately 5  of the cells  A cyclin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  stain is negative  Overall  the findings are consistent with a portion of normal lymph node with primary follicles  A single detached cluster of atypical epithelial cells is noted in blood clot separate from the lymph node on a keratin immunohistochemical stain  Although not present on the initial H E levels  this cluster is present on a deeper H  br level  Further studies to better characterize these epithelial cells and the relationship to the patient s known breast carcinoma are pending and will be reported in an addendum  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  are three cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm which are submitted in toto as cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Robert Hasserjian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE NOTE  Using immunoperoxidase methods  the atypical epithelial cell clusters are negative for GCDFP 15  Nevertheless  this detached fragment does resemble the tumor cells seen in the prior core biopsy   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and sentinel lymph node biopsy   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and Her2 neu protein expression and fluorescence in situ hybridization studies for Her2 neu gene amplification were performed on the sentinel lymph node specimen and reported in an addendum to that case   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Addendum  1 by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY  report_end  , Negative.
